Procurement implementation plan: from fee proposal to award
16 Oct 2026 · @Ben clifton 
Summary
Fee proposals and tender submissions are dropped into the document repository like any other file. Jev recognises them as commercial documents, works out the discipline and the firm, and they appear in that package's firm columns on the procurement page with the firm's details filled in. Prices are read into the same schedule the RFP asked for, so two or more submissions line up in one comparison table, followed by a short non-price section and a recommendation. Awarding a firm writes its fee breakdown into the cost plan as child lines under one parent, which is what later invoices map to.
The recommended order is to get one proposal all the way from drop to cost plan before building the multi-firm report. Comparison then mostly renders data that already exists, and the only LLM call arrives last.
