Why one proposal end to end first. Small residential jobs often have a single fee proposal, so award-to-cost-plan is useful without any comparison. It also proves the hardest parts first: reading fees reliably, and the schedule-to-cost-plan link that the invoice feature depends on. Once one proposal reads cleanly, comparing three is the same extraction run three times plus a table.
Why the LLM comes last. Price evaluation is arithmetic and lookups, so code and Jev do it faster and more reliably. The LLM is only needed to summarise non-price answers and draft the recommendation, which is also the part the owner must approve under the "Jev only" rule in AGENTS.md.
