Price items are read from the PM's selections in that section, never hard-coded per discipline. The owner plans to refine the scope by stage and fee proposal section for each discipline, and those changes must flow through to comparison and award with no code change.
The returnable schedules (R2, R3, R4, R5 and so on) are currently a block of text in the RFP. This phase renders each one as a table for the firm to fill in, with the same content. The coding agent may adjust their wording so the RFP, the extraction and the report line up item for item. Tables also make proposals easier to read, because firms tend to answer in the structure they were given.
Each item has a stable id, a label, an order and its kind. The discipline template supplies a default schedule, so a proposal that arrives without an issued RFP still has rows to be read into.
