Phase 2: price extraction and the price table
Price reading runs as a background job straight after filing, so it never slows the drop. It follows the usual split: code harvests and computes, Jev only picks.
1. Harvest (code). Collect every money amount with its row label from tables and text, plus stated totals, GST wording (inc or ex), hourly rates, percentage fees, and the exclusions and assumptions sections.
2. Map (Jev). For each price and rate item in the schedule, one choice question: which harvested amount answers this item? The options are the candidates plus Not priced and Included in another item. All items go out in one parallel fan-out.
3. Leftovers (code). Amounts that no item claimed and that aren't totals become Other items for that firm, so nothing offered is lost.
4. Check (code). Normalise everything to ex GST, compare the sum of mapped items to the firm's stated total, and flag any gap.
5. Review (user). Every cell shows its band chip and opens the source passage in the PDF. A user's correction is final.
The price table is one screen for both cases: with one firm it is the review screen, with several it is the comparison. Firms run across the top and schedule items down the left, answering the two first questions: did everyone price everything, and who is cheapest. Example layout, with illustrative figures:
