Phase 4: non-price and the one-page report
This phase adds the first LLM to SiteWise, so the owner first amends non-negotiable #1 in AGENTS.md, for example: "Jev decides; code computes. A generative model may only draft prose from evidence that Jev and code selected, must cite it, and never sets a field or a number."
Before the call. Code splits each proposal into sections by its headings. For each non-price criterion and each firm, Jev picks which sections answer it, or none. Code also collects each firm's departures, exclusions and assumptions passages.
The one call. One request per report, to a fast, low-cost model hosted in an Australian region. It receives the price table's computed facts and the selected passages with their ids, and must return JSON in a fixed schema:
• a summary of at most 25 words per criterion per firm, citing passage ids;
• each firm's departures from the RFP, citing passage ids;
• a recommendation of at most 120 words.
After the call, code checks it. Every cited id must exist, every summary must cite something, and every dollar figure or number in the text must match a computed value or appear in a cited passage. Anything that fails is dropped and flagged rather than shown. The result is cached by a hash of its inputs and regenerated only when a submission changes. If the call fails or times out, the report still renders with the price section and the raw passages under each criterion.
Ratings stay with the PM. The model does not score firms, and there are no weights or numeric scores. The PM sets a rating per criterion per firm (Strong, Acceptable or Concern) and edits the recommendation, which is labelled "Drafted by model, edited by" with their name.
The report is one page of A4 landscape, two at most. For now it is an in-app page with a print layout; it moves to proper PDF and Word export when the app-wide export feature is built:
1. Header: project, package, RFP reference, date and the firms compared.
2. Price: the Phase 2 table, unchanged.
3. Non-price: criteria down the left, firms across, a short summary and rating in each cell, departures as the last row.
4. Recommendation: the edited paragraph and the PM's sign-off.
